<article class="guide-article bg-canvas py-12 md:py-16" aria-label="Wi-Fi dropout diagnosis guide">
  <div class="guide-reading mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-lg">
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A video call freezes in the study, but the television keeps streaming. Or every device loses access at once. Both experiences get called “bad Wi-Fi”, yet they give someone investigating the problem different places to start.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">You do not need to buy another booster or become a network technician before asking for help. Start with a few observations you can repeat and explain. They may help you solve a simple problem yourself, or make a conversation with your provider or a local technician more useful.</p>
{% include "components/guide-start.njk" %}
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Separate the parts of the connection</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Your device connects over Wi-Fi to your home router. The router connects your home network to your internet service. The website or application you are using is another part of the experience. A connection to the local network does not necessarily mean the internet is available; an individual app can also have trouble while the connection works. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/experience/connectivity-networking/fix-wi-fi-connection-issues-in-windows">Microsoft explains these connection states</a>.</p>
<figure class="guide-diagram"><figcaption class="guide-kicker">The connection path · a simplified map</figcaption><ol aria-label="Connection path"><li>Device</li><li>Wi-Fi</li><li>Router</li><li>Internet service</li><li>Website or app</li></ol><p>This map helps describe the symptom. It is not a test that identifies a faulty component.</p></figure>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Make a small comparison</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Choose one familiar activity, such as opening an ordinary website. Note what happened, then compare one thing at a time:</p>
<div class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto" role="region" aria-label="Wi-Fi dropout diagnosis guide comparison table" tabindex="0"><table role="table" class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm md:text-base">
<thead>
<tr role="row">
<th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Comparison</th>
<th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Useful question to record</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr role="row">
<td role="cell" data-label="Comparison" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Another device on the same home Wi-Fi</td>
<td role="cell" data-label="Useful question to record" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Does it have the same problem at about the same time?</td>
</tr>
<tr role="row">
<td role="cell" data-label="Comparison" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">The same device in another room</td>
<td role="cell" data-label="Useful question to record" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Does the experience change near the router?</td>
</tr>
<tr role="row">
<td role="cell" data-label="Comparison" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Another familiar website or app</td>
<td role="cell" data-label="Useful question to record" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Is the difficulty limited to one service?</td>
</tr>
<tr role="row">
<td role="cell" data-label="Comparison" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">The same activity later</td>
<td role="cell" data-label="Useful question to record" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Is the problem continuous or intermittent?</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Microsoft recommends checking another device on the same network as part of troubleshooting. That comparison is a clue, not proof that a particular device needs replacing. Make sure you are comparing the same home Wi-Fi rather than a phone's mobile connection. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/experience/connectivity-networking/fix-wi-fi-connection-issues-in-windows">See Microsoft's troubleshooting guidance</a>.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Do not spend an afternoon changing everything. Two or three clear observations are more useful than a long list of adjustments whose effects you cannot separate.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For a step-by-step comparison and help describing the result, read <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/wifi-one-device-or-all/">Wi-Fi trouble on one device or every device?</a></p>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">When a speed test is useful</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A connection test gives you something to compare. nbn suggests testing beside the router, comparing with an Ethernet connection to the router where practical, and testing Wi-Fi in other rooms. Differences between rooms can point toward a coverage or placement issue. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://www.nbnco.com.au/learn/optimisation/what-to-look-for-in-a-wifi-router">Read nbn's test and interpretation guidance</a>.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Use the test your internet provider directs you to, record its name, and keep the device and test consistent. Note the time, room and whether the connection was Wi-Fi or Ethernet. Keep the units shown with the result. Do not move unfamiliar cabling or connect directly to an nbn box to follow this article; skip a wired comparison if you are unsure.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Treat the result as an observation from that moment. Avoid turning one number into “the router is broken” or “we need a faster plan”. Bring your notes to the provider or technician so the result can be considered with the symptoms.</p>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Keep a short dropout diary</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Copy this into a note on your own device or onto paper:</p>
<blockquote class="guide-note"><span class="guide-kicker">Example note</span>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">At [time], I was using [device] in [room] for [activity]. The problem lasted about [duration]. Another device [had the same problem / worked / was not checked]. I saw [connection message]. This has happened [pattern]. The test I used was [name], and its result was [value and units].</p>
</blockquote>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">You can leave any field blank. You do not need to include passwords, authentication codes, account numbers or private documents. If you share a screenshot, check what else it reveals first.</p>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">What to do with the pattern</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If the problem follows a room, mention that. If it affects several devices together, say so. If only one program fails, name it. These are useful starting points for investigation; none obliges you to buy equipment.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For service outages or continuing internet-service concerns, contact your provider. For uncertainty about your home setup, a scoped diagnosis can help separate service, router, placement, interference and coverage questions. Avoid factory resets or disabling security settings just to see what happens. If you cannot confidently reverse a change, pause and ask for help.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If ordinary computer tasks also feel slow, our <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://nakedtech.au/guides/slow-computer-fix-upgrade-replace/">fix, upgrade or replace guide</a> can help you organise that separate question.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For a side-by-side comparison, read <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/slow-computer-or-internet/">Is your computer slow, or is the internet slow?</a>.</p>
